  "body": "## Why\n\nThe user asked to see the flutes in the 3D model preview. The maintainer wrote: \"as long as we keep the 3D preview bit, im aiming to develop on that down the line / as running weirdly shape tools requires models / not just a spun profile\".\n\n## What changed\n\n- The 3D preview of the tool library window cuts helical flute grooves into the fluted length of the revolved model (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tool_library_dialog/flutes.rs`, new).\n  - Count: the stated `flutes`, 1 to 16. No stated count gives no flutes.\n  - Helix: `catalog.helix_deg`, 0 to 80 degrees. The value 0, no value, or a value out of range gives straight flutes. The helix is right-hand: the twist is `z * tan(helix) / R`.\n  - Groove: a sine section on 45 % of each flute pitch. The floor is 60 % of the local radius, so a groove fades at a ball tip and at a drill point. The grooves run out over the top 8 % of the fluted length.\n  - Kinds with flutes: end mill, ball nose, bull nose, twist drill, chamfer mill. All other kinds (tap, thread mills, form mill, T-slot, keyseat, dovetail, lollipop, turning, EDM, plasma, waterjet, wire, probe) show the plain model.\n- A \"Flutes\" toggle follows \"Dimensions\" and \"Holder\" (view state, starts on). The toggle queues no command. The row can wrap in a narrow preview, and the drawing then takes the height that is left.\n- `ToolModel` keeps `fluted` and `fluted_bare` next to the plain meshes. `ToolModel::shown(holder, flutes)` picks the mesh. The view box is the box of the plain mesh, so a toggle does not move the view.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/3908-tool-preview-flutes.md`.\n\n## Display-only rule (safety)\n\n- The fluted mesh is built in a private module (`mod flutes`, not `pub`) of `crates/ui`. No crate below `ui` (app, sim, motion, post, tools) can name it.\n- The steel outline, the holder bands of the collision check, the plain meshes, `Tool::geom` and `Tool::profile` do not change with the flutes. Pinned by `the_flutes_do_not_change_what_the_checks_read`.\n- Each fluted point is on or inside the revolved envelope (a groove only removes radius). Pinned by `the_fluted_steel_stays_inside_the_revolved_envelope`.\n\n## Triangle bound\n\n96 facets around. The fluted length has 16 to 64 rings (one ring for each 0.12 rad of twist). A meridian with more than 120 points gets no flutes. The fluted steel has at most 2 * 96 * 119 = 22,848 facets. A `const` assertion checks that this is not more than the painted budget of the model view (`MAX_PAINTED` = 30,000), and the build refuses a larger mesh. Reading (computed from the rule, not measured): the seeded Ø 6 end mill with 4 flutes and a 30 degree helix has 24 rings and about 5,200 facets of fluted steel.\n\n## Frame cost\n\nThe fluted meshes are built with the rest of the model, on the same key (the draft tool value, which holds `flutes` and the helix). A still frame builds nothing and projects nothing. A changed helix builds the model one time. The toggle builds nothing: it picks a mesh that is already built, and the projection cache projects the new pick one time.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `flutes::tests::an_end_mill_shows_its_flute_count_on_the_fluted_length` (2, 3, 4 and 6 flutes; the groove floor is the core; the shank is plain)\n- `flutes::tests::helix_zero_cuts_straight_grooves_and_a_helix_twists_them`\n- `flutes::tests::the_fluted_steel_stays_inside_the_revolved_envelope`\n- `flutes::tests::tools_without_flutes_draw_the_plain_model`\n- `flutes::tests::the_fluted_steel_keeps_to_its_facet_bound`\n- `tool_library_preview::the_flutes_toggle_shows_and_hides_the_helical_flutes` (no command, a plain model when off, the same holder)\n- `tool_library_preview::the_flutes_do_not_change_what_the_checks_read`\n- `tool_library_preview::a_changed_helix_rebuilds_the_fluted_model_once` (a still frame computes no mesh)\n- `page_layout_tool_library::layout_window_tool_editor` (updated: Flutes follows Holder on its row or wraps under it, inside the window)\n\nThe ui lib `#[test]` count goes from 1656 to 1664 (8 new tests, none removed). No snapshot PNG changes. Each changed file has fewer than 400 lines.\n\n## Gate (Windows, winbuild)\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` on head `a3dee508f` (log `C:\\camcraft-logs\\gate-3908-a3dee508f.log`, first line `HEAD: a3dee508f5dbb28025c09b507bbae5830fec7939`):\n\n```\n  ok     229s  ui build (--no-run)\n  ok     121s  ui suites: lib\n  ok  (16 more ui suites: boundary .. waterjet_tool, 1-3 s each)\n  wall 6.6 min, 18 step(s), 0 failed, 0 stalled\n```\n\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` on the same head: clean (exit 0). Only `camcraft-ui` changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The live app with a mouse (the screenshots come from the headless egui_kittest renderer).\n- A tool with an imported body that is also fluted (the revolved steel below a body gets the flutes; the body is drawn as it is).\n- No post, toolpath or check code changed, so no example catalog suite and no light lane apply.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nHolder off in each view, so that the cutter is larger. \"Before\" is main `10ea81a2a`; \"after\" is head `a3dee508f`.\n\n| | Before (main) | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| End mill, 4 flutes, 30° | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3908/before-endmill-4fl-30deg.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3908/after-endmill-4fl-30deg.png) |\n| Ball mill, 2 flutes, 30° | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3908/before-ballmill-2fl-30deg.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3908/after-ballmill-2fl-30deg.png) |\n\n| Helix 0 (straight) | Flutes toggle off | 3 flutes, 45°, holder on |\n|---|---|---|\n| ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3908/after-endmill-4fl-helix0.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3908/after-endmill-flutes-off.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3908/after-endmill-3fl-45deg-holder.png) |\n\nChangelog: The 3D tool preview shows helical flutes on end, ball and bull nose mills, drills and chamfer mills (the flute count and the helix angle; display only), with a Flutes toggle.\n\nEffort: medium\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #3908\n",
